{"id": "clm:a0ec32f3f564c44099bfdea0f4c069625c7ec1478a88d528a553749ebb34b3e6", "type": "statement", "text": "NIST states that the initial EWMA plays an important role in subsequent EWMA values. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/pmc/section4/pmc431.htm", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Exponentially weighted baselines for streaming probability forecasts"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:9c95f51058cb365f9af80164fa13f1693d48542b8fe90b31605838d46550a047", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a99a37e9baae78b2f38cde6f2529e5cb293408565568fde5a22537bf8bf7597b"]}
{"id": "clm:47fa79e002947fbde9db95282022e3be4755d59dad5deda3990c55746b069d5d", "type": "statement", "text": "Stanford authors describe an EWMA as recursively computable without storing all past values, with per-step effort that does not grow over time. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2404.08136v2", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Exponentially weighted baselines for streaming probability forecasts"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:9c95f51058cb365f9af80164fa13f1693d48542b8fe90b31605838d46550a047", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:8160b7501f9f69d888be3e158280e4c82b12c14ad1ff0d2b14838bb36f25c218", "ev:9abcaa7b8cabf4d0ed096787d2456966cb50cbea8a1e859191dc7effca911586"]}
{"id": "clm:a91888b1f40f0820ad857256a2b95c66eebc6242f895608f2a21dd9b23a68bbd", "type": "statement", "text": "For a general exponentially weighted moving model, the Stanford authors state that an exact simple recursion need not be available. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2404.08136v2", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Exponentially weighted baselines for streaming probability forecasts"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:9c95f51058cb365f9af80164fa13f1693d48542b8fe90b31605838d46550a047", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:9abcaa7b8cabf4d0ed096787d2456966cb50cbea8a1e859191dc7effca911586", "ev:a0548e7c84c87fceed8cce64f0d502b21a75946f511efa11a16f5db0bd5e0ad4"]}
{"id": "clm:c68951070a405edd3b72251a68b13fa6eb25124bd2904950b006eb5034845a11", "type": "statement", "text": "NIST defines single exponential smoothing recursively as S_t = α y_(t−1) + (1−α) S_(t−1), for 0 < α ≤ 1 and t ≥ 3. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/pmc/section4/pmc431.htm", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Exponentially weighted baselines for streaming probability forecasts"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:9c95f51058cb365f9af80164fa13f1693d48542b8fe90b31605838d46550a047", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:7d2026362753260d6f8086a8bd44a3f0a7a8c11ed2b5cc93636f5b60063c8a5d"]}
{"id": "clm:a81d53c81431ba34396a39c41da632a715b29576439e6acf71df112f31fedf59", "type": "statement", "text": "NIST describes exponential smoothing as weighting past observations with exponentially decreasing weights for forecasting. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/pmc/section4/pmc431.htm", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Exponentially weighted baselines for streaming probability forecasts"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:9c95f51058cb365f9af80164fa13f1693d48542b8fe90b31605838d46550a047", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5589aec48fc7937e3299c882eb2002ac6cc838170d4583efac13b4e4b72c628e"]}
{"id": "clm:87b58a6dc00402a11b6f96be728e3340db029ba099b8278f3b54aa49c7b1ce77", "type": "statement", "text": "NIST states that selection of the initial EWMA becomes more important as the smoothing parameter α decreases. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/pmc/section4/pmc431.htm", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Exponentially weighted baselines for streaming probability forecasts"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:9c95f51058cb365f9af80164fa13f1693d48542b8fe90b31605838d46550a047", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0b4c5fb8e760ba5426e98d2081bed52487aa47fd1ba9d313639f48cefd10cabf"]}
{"id": "clm:bf30f2028794aeea4762b375323e98f890060077dc24d08463c55f65ec0b5024", "type": "statement", "text": "The Stanford authors describe the half-life of their exponentially weighted model as the number of periods over which a weight decays to one-half. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2404.08136v2", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Exponentially weighted baselines for streaming probability forecasts"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:9c95f51058cb365f9af80164fa13f1693d48542b8fe90b31605838d46550a047", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2eed47263b5e1bfabfb5aa978d1947c636b6cb4480f8985441663730d3241868", "ev:9abcaa7b8cabf4d0ed096787d2456966cb50cbea8a1e859191dc7effca911586"]}
{"id": "clm:fb0fcc9727d6efd2084a03718b950beae02b1764035cdb95eae4600225e0b9b7", "type": "statement", "text": "In the cited pandas documentation, ignore_na=False bases exponential weights on absolute positions. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.Series.ewm.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Exponentially weighted baselines for streaming probability forecasts"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:9c95f51058cb365f9af80164fa13f1693d48542b8fe90b31605838d46550a047", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0ef15545d38d6af16638d6461a91f3f7441f6d5a1a9825c588be6554df405a5e"]}
{"id": "clm:a6ef160ba68d0d3db0f96c03ed6237a5be69c6c6081a5337ca621cf4a1b61d41", "type": "statement", "text": "In the cited pandas documentation, ignore_na=True bases exponential weights on relative positions. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.Series.ewm.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Exponentially weighted baselines for streaming probability forecasts"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:9c95f51058cb365f9af80164fa13f1693d48542b8fe90b31605838d46550a047", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:aa3b2cbb91f33915af24e4ff4c56d850a8143664e714b669735cc7f6668bd18d"]}
{"id": "clm:40897db80e2d38de63092c2d92a3dad839c9e23b44fd1f8e30307f245747e4a8", "type": "statement", "text": "In the cited pandas documentation, adjust=False uses a recursive exponentially weighted calculation. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.Series.ewm.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Exponentially weighted baselines for streaming probability forecasts"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:9c95f51058cb365f9af80164fa13f1693d48542b8fe90b31605838d46550a047", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4a30840bdaa4e9085220a36795c09e6a4cce48ad9d1db979e4d6fc616b6eb695"]}
{"id": "clm:bc8951fa264d27f624c1922ea2d18ebe9367c56508db2e089f03dc8150c0d6c5", "type": "statement", "text": "The exponentially weighted prediction preprint includes Bernoulli observations among its exponential-family examples. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2512.16745v3", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Exponentially weighted baselines for streaming probability forecasts"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:9c95f51058cb365f9af80164fa13f1693d48542b8fe90b31605838d46550a047", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1e65f215111a7533b6184d7615ae608730d79235feeda8a8bcb0bda519a3a4c5"]}
{"id": "clm:0d2a1114f5ad6b07eaf508dc92de924c7c1bbfdc757fdd85e668d36f386290c5", "type": "statement", "text": "Pandas documents an adjustment factor for early exponentially weighted calculations to account for imbalance in relative weights. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.Series.ewm.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Exponentially weighted baselines for streaming probability forecasts"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:9c95f51058cb365f9af80164fa13f1693d48542b8fe90b31605838d46550a047", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a0ae84dae6c948e1d7435c5283738d37a46e2e83158b44abc0d2c8d1bee5f207"]}
